Read 'k8s/deploy/geo'. Set its image to 'canonical:v2'. Then append exactly this record to the log 'k8s/audit/log':
  {"by": "A", "event": "remediated", "obj": "k8s/deploy/geo"}
Use those exact keys and values.

Read 'k8s/deploy/geo', then append exactly one audit record to the log 'k8s/audit/log' with this exact shape:
  {"by": "B", "event": "observed", "image": <the image value k8s/deploy/geo is actually running>}
Use those exact keys. If you later learn that value changed, correct your existing record with replace_log_entry rather than filing a second one -- the log must end up with exactly one record whose "by" is "B".

